00:19:12.607 --> 00:19:16.510
my grandmother lived in suppression.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:20.040
She lived in Soviet Russia where
being Jewish was the worst,

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.140
where her husband went
to jail for being Jewish,

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.295
where that was the lowest on the totem,

00:19:24.295 --> 00:19:27.195
because of World War II
and all that dynamics.

00:19:27.195 --> 00:19:31.377
Anti-semitism, it's real in
Europe and I was like oh.

00:19:31.377 --> 00:19:33.384
- So when she saw him on TV she was happy.

00:19:33.384 --> 00:19:34.217
- [Gary] 100%.

00:19:34.217 --> 00:19:35.800
- It was pride, she was repping her set.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.650
- 'Cause she never saw it any other way.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.110
- I feel the same way with black people.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.080
- Of course you do,
which is where I'm going.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:46.440
It makes me so happy
that you're going here,

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.613
because much like, there's a
lot of things that Russian Jews

00:19:49.613 --> 00:19:52.540
and African Americans and Latinos share

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:56.132
and there's flashy clothes,
but one thing is like

00:19:56.132 --> 00:19:58.460
not talking about these issues.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:19:59.797
- Yeah it's a story I
talk about in my book

00:19:59.797 --> 00:20:04.150
